cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "AEGIS-AT: Attribution Integrity Benchmark for Multi-Agent Delegation"
message: "If you use this software or its findings, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Singh
    given-names: Rahul
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/XXXX-XXXX-XXXX-XXXX"   # add once you register an ORCID (recommended)
repository-code: "https://github.com/rahulsingh1397/aegis-at"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible, pre-registered adversarial benchmark measuring whether
  OAuth 2.0 Token Exchange (RFC 8693) delegation preserves audit attribution
  in multi-agent AI systems. v1 shows attribution regresses when delegation is
  added (the standard records the requester, not the executor); v2 measures the
  standardized fix (DPoP / RFC 9449 sender-constrained tokens recover
  attribution), adds a Log Integrity Score, a 3-agent multi-hop topology, and
  stochastic Wilson confidence intervals.
license: Apache-2.0
version: "v2.0.1"
date-released: "2026-06-14"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.20693303"
keywords:
  - multi-agent systems
  - AI agent security
  - attribution
  - non-repudiation
  - RFC 8693
  - DPoP
  - sender-constrained tokens
  - confused deputy
  - benchmark
